  "id": "ms-azure-local-hyperconverged-platform-v1",
  "title": "Connected Azure Local hyperconverged platform",
  "subtitle": "A connected 2–16 machine Azure Local cluster combines local compute and storage with Azure Arc-based cloud management. Synthetic Azure reference; no deployment is implied.",
  "description": "### Problem\nOrganizations may need local workload execution and storage while using Azure for centralized governance, monitoring, security, and lifecycle management.\n\n### Flow and Azure mapping\nValidated physical machines connect through redundant top-of-rack switches and an upstream corporate network. The Azure Local instance provides Hyper-V and Storage Spaces Direct; workloads run as VMs or supported Kubernetes deployments. Azure Arc connects the instance to Azure management services, while Azure Monitor, Key Vault, Defender for Cloud, and backup/recovery services remain cloud-hosted. Management traffic and workload traffic should be distinguished from the local east-west storage path.\n\n### Trade-offs and assumptions\nThe source describes a connected, storage-switched baseline for 2–16 machines; it excludes single-machine, disconnected, switchless, rack-aware, and disaggregated designs. Hardware validation, networking, update cadence, and workload sizing are prerequisites. Do not depict Azure monitoring or policy agents as on-premises services unless the selected configuration explicitly supports that deployment.\n\nSource: [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/hybrid/azure-local-baseline).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- Origin provider: Microsoft\n- Target: Azure conceptual adaptation\n- Primary source: [Azure Local Hyperconverged Baseline Reference Architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/hybrid/azure-local-baseline)\n- Reviewed: 2026-11-06\n\n## Catalog status\n\nThis is an original, editable Azure conceptual adaptation. It is synthetic reference material, not a deployed system, certified vendor architecture, or automatic deployment plan.\n\n## Mapping caveats\n\n- The reference excludes disconnected operations and a single-node design; do not imply Azure management services execute locally.",
